      <title>Elements in Indiana's toxic coal ash worth billions, could still be too expensive to mine</title>
      <link>https://www.ipm.org/news/2026-01-08/elements-in-indianas-toxic-coal-ash-worth-billions-could-still-be-too-expensive-to-mine</link>
      <description>Recovering rare earth elements from toxic coal ash could be a win-win for Indiana’s environment and its economy. These are used in things like electric vehicle batteries, medical equipment, jet engines and wind turbines. A new report shows Indiana has a long way to go before extracting those elements is profitable.</description>
